    "title": "LESSON 30: SPEAKING TO THE MANY",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "A continent of peoples means speaking",
          "to groups. Commands and thanks take",
          "the plural ending -eni (Lesson 25);",
          "the greeting swaps its WHO bead:",
          "",
          "   Karibuni!     Welcome, all of you!",
          "   Asanteni!     Thank you all!",
          "   Hamjambo?     Nothing wrong with",
          "                 you all?",
          "   Hatujambo!    Nothing wrong with us!",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "Lesson 2's ceremony, now sized for",
          "a room instead of a person."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Karibuni! Asanteni! Hamjambo? Hatujambo!"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Respect rides on titles, not on \"you\":",
          "",
          "   Wewe forms, to one person;",
          "   ninyi forms, to a group.",
          "",
          "Respect to one elder is shown with",
          "titles and greetings, not the plural:",
          "",
          "   Shikamoo, mzee.  (to one elder)",
          "   Shikamooni!      (to elders together)",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "When unsure, greet up: no one was",
          "ever insulted by respect."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Shikamoo, mzee. Shikamooni!"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
