    "lesson_id": "032",
    "trigger_word": "hifadhi",
    "trigger_card_number": 1,
    "title": "LESSON 32: IF AND WHILE: -KI-",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Weather teaches conditionals. The",
          "-ki- bead is Lesson 19's kama,",
          "compressed into the verb:",
          "",
          "   Mvua ikinyesha, tunakaa ndani.",
          "   If it rains, we stay inside.",
          "",
          "   Ukienda sasa, utafika mapema.",
          "   If you go now, you'll arrive early.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "WHO + ki + ROOT — no tense of its",
          "own; the main clause carries time."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Mvua ikinyesha, tunakaa ndani. Ukienda sasa, utafika mapema."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The same bead also paints an action",
          "in progress alongside another:",
          "",
          "   Niliwaona watoto wakicheza.",
          "   I saw the children playing.",
          "",
          "   Tulikaa tukisubiri mvua.",
          "   We sat waiting for the rain.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "If-ness and while-ness in one bead:",
          "both read as 'the situation being",
          "so'. Context — as ever in Swahili —",
          "does the rest."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Niliwaona watoto wakicheza. Tulikaa tukisubiri mvua."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
